  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="Transformer model architecture (discarded)">
      <data key="d0">Transformer model architecture (discarded)</data>
      <data key="d1">discarded</data>
      <data key="d2">This discarded content provides a detailed description of the Transformer model architecture, which is a new approach to sequence modeling and transduction. The Transformer model architecture is based on self-attention mechanisms and does not rely on recurrence or convolution, which allows for more parallelization and improved computational efficiency. The architecture consists of stacked self-attention and point-wise, fully connected layers for both the encoder and decoder, and uses Multi-Head Attention to reduce the number of operations required to relate signals from two arbitrary input or output positions. The Transformer model is designed to achieve a new state of the art in translation quality after being trained for as little as twelve hours on eight P100 GPUs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-eff53e9331bf98ce9f7fd979f7fa2ddc</data>
      <data key="d4">attention.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763824580</data>
    </node>
    <node id="unknown_entity (unknown)">
